{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.reidemeister_action_table","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.reidemeister_action_table","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.reidemeister_action_table","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.reidemeister_action_table","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L75-L173","doc":"**Manuscript statement** (full body):\n\nEvery braid move acts on the three sectors of the categorical\naction $\\mathfrak{S}_q = \\mathfrak{S}_q^{\\mathrm{grav}} + \\mathfrak{S}_q^{\\mathrm{gauge}} + \\mathfrak{S}_q^{\\mathrm{matter}}$\n([canonical action](#prop:qou-canonical-action)).  This table\ngives the complete accounting: what each move preserves, what it\nchanges, and what must be tracked for mass and energy calculations.\n\n**The categorical action on a nuclear link.**\nFor a nucleus $\\mathcal{N}(Z, N)$ evaluated at the braid\nrepresentative $\\beta \\in B_A$:\n\n$$\n  \\mathfrak{S}_q[\\beta]\n  = \n  \\underbrace{E_0}_{\\text{gravity}}\n  + \n  \\underbrace{\\sum_{\\text{crossings}} \\mathcal{S}_{ij}(q)}_{\\text{gauge}}\n  + \n  \\underbrace{\\mathfrak{S}_q^{\\mathrm{matter}}}_{\\text{matter (Pauli + pairing)}}\n$$\n\nThe gauge sector decomposes via the Iwahori--Hecke algebra:\neach crossing $\\sigma_i$ contributes weight $q$ (positive),\n$q^{-1}$ (negative), or $(q + q^{-1})/2$ (mixed).\n\n**Complete move table.**\n\n```tex\n\\begin{center}\n\\renewcommand{\\arraystretch}{1.4}\n\\begin{tabular}{l|c|c|c|c|c|c}\n\\toprule\n\\textbf{Move} & \\textbf{Algebra} &\n  $\\mathcal{S}^{\\mathrm{grav}}$ &\n  $\\mathcal{S}^{\\mathrm{gauge}}$ &\n  $\\mathcal{S}^{\\mathrm{matter}}$ &\n  \\textbf{Vol} & \\textbf{tr} \\\\\n\\midrule\nR1 (self-twist) &\n  $\\sigma_i \\mapsto \\sigma_i \\sigma_n$ &\n  $0$ &\n  $+q \\text{ or } +q^{-1}$ &\n  $0$ &\n  \\textbf{changes} &\n  $\\times z$ \\\\\n\\midrule\nR2 ($q$-deformed) &\n  $\\sigma_i^2 = (q{-}q^{-1})\\sigma_i + 1$ &\n  $0$ &\n  \\textbf{splits:} $(q{-}q^{-1})\\sigma + 1$ &\n  $0$ &\n  \\textbf{changes} &\n  \\textbf{changes} \\\\\n\\midrule\nR2 (classical) &\n  $\\sigma_i \\sigma_i^{-1} = 1$ &\n  $0$ &\n  $0$ (cancels) &\n  $0$ &\n  preserved &\n  preserved \\\\\n\\midrule\nR3 (Yang--Baxter) &\n  $\\sigma_i\\sigma_{i+1}\\sigma_i$\n  $= \\sigma_{i+1}\\sigma_i\\sigma_{i+1}$ &\n  $0$ &\n  $0$ &\n  $0$ &\n  preserved &\n  preserved \\\\\n\\midrule\nFar comm. &\n  $\\sigma_i\\sigma_j = \\sigma_j\\sigma_i$ &\n  $0$ &\n  $0$ &\n  $0$ &\n  preserved &\n  preserved \\\\\n\\midrule\nMarkov I &\n  $\\beta \\mapsto \\gamma\\beta\\gamma^{-1}$ \n\n[…truncated; see manuscript for remainder…]\n\n    The Lean encoding below splits the manuscript claim into named\n    sub-claim fields; concretisation requires per-block manuscript\n    translation. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:reidemeister-action-table","label":"prop:reidemeister-action-table","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/reidemeister-action-table.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_markov_II_stabilisation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_markov_II_stabilisation","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L73-L73","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (M-II) — Markov-II stabilisation\n`β ↦ β · σ_n` multiplies the trace by `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_MII","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_MII","kind":"def","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L70-L70","doc":"The Markov-II stabilised braid `β · σ_n` (positive case). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_markov_I_conjugation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_markov_I_conjugation","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (M-I) — Markov-I conjugation preserves\nthe trace (cyclicity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_MI","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_MI","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L65-L65","doc":"The Markov-I conjugate `γ β γ⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_far_commute","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_far_commute","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L63-L63","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (FarComm) — `σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i` (|i − j| ≥ 2)\npreserves the trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_FC","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_FC","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L60-L60","doc":"The braid after applying a far-commute swap. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_r3_yang_baxter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_r3_yang_baxter","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (R3) — Yang-Baxter\n`σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i = σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}` preserves the trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_R3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_R3","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The braid after applying R3 Yang-Baxter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_r2_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_r2_classical","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (R2-classical) — `σ_i σ_i⁻¹ = 1` is the\nidentity move; trace is preserved exactly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_R2c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_R2c","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L50-L50","doc":"The braid after applying R2-classical `σ_i σ_i⁻¹ = 1` (= original). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_r2_q_deformed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_r2_q_deformed","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L47-L47","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (R2-q) — `q`-deformed second Reidemeister\nmove splits the trace as `tr(σ²β) = (q − q⁻¹)·tr(σβ) + tr(β)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_R2q_split_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_R2q_split_two","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_R2q_split_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_R2q_split_one","kind":"def","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L43-L43","doc":"The two braids resulting from the q-deformed R2 split\n`σ_i² = (q − q⁻¹)σ_i + 1`: one with single crossing, one trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_r1_self_twist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.claim_r1_self_twist","kind":"theorem","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L40-L40","doc":"Manuscript sub-claim (R1) — self-twist `β ↦ β · σ_n` scales the\nMarkov trace by `z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_R1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β_R1","kind":"def","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L37-L37","doc":"The braid after applying an R1 self-twist `β ↦ β · σ_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.β","kind":"def","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L35-L35","doc":"The base braid `β` whose moves we're tracking. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.trM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.trM","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L33-L33","doc":"Markov-trace function on braids `tr_M : Braid → ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.Braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.Braid","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L31-L31","doc":"Braid representative type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.z","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L29-L29","doc":"Markov parameter `z = 1/(q^{1/2} + q^{-1/2})`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.q","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L27-L27","doc":"Substrate parameter `q : ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.N","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.N","kind":"def","line":25,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L25-L25","doc":"Neutron number `N`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.Z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.Z","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L23-L23","doc":"Proton number `Z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L21-L21","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.ReidemeisterActionTableContext","kind":"class","line":17,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/reidemeister_action_table.lean#L17-L73","doc":"Abstract context for the `reidemeister_action_table` claim —\nmanuscript-themed typed fields below; sub-claims map to the rows of\nthe manuscript table (each Reidemeister / Markov move's behaviour on\nthe three action sectors plus volume and trace). ","signatureChunk":0}]}